  "habitat": "Groups on fynbos-covered hillsides, including coastal suburbia, and on Karoo hills and montane foothills. The colour key says fynbos and eastern mountain foothills. The male calls from a high perch and is aggressive to other males.",
  "summary": "A common resident. A large, all-green sunbird with a long tail. The breeding male is entirely iridescent green except for blue-black wings and tail. The non-breeding male is yellow below, variably speckled with green. The female is told by large size and a long bill. The call is chew-chew-chew, chi-chi-chi-chiew, chit-chit-chit, with a rapid warbling song. Newman gives no length. That description is printed on the Amethyst page. No Kemp estimate is stored.",
